Given, magnification \(m = \frac{1}{4}\). The distance between the object and its image is 40 cm.
m = -\frac{v}{u}
Since the magnification is positive and less than 1, it implies a virtual, erect, and diminished image, which is formed by a convex mirror. For a convex mirror, the object distance \(u\) is negative and the image distance \(v\) is positive. The magnification can be written as \(m = \frac{|v|}{|u|}\).
\frac{1}{4} = \frac{v}{|u|} \Rightarrow |u| = 4v
The distance between the object and its image for a convex mirror is \(|u| + v = 40\).
v + 4v = 40
5v = 40
v = 8 \text{ cm}
|u| = 4 \times 8 = 32 \text{ cm}
Now, applying the mirror formula \(\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{v} + \frac{1}{u}\) with proper sign conventions for a convex mirror (\(v = +8\) cm and \(u = -32\) cm):
\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{-32}
\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{8} - \frac{1}{32}
\frac{1}{f} = \frac{4 - 1}{32}
\frac{1}{f} = \frac{3}{32}
f = \frac{32}{3} = 10.66... \approx 10.7 \text{ cm}

